---
// Terms of sale (English translation, for information; the French version prevails).
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import Val from '../../components/legal/Val.astro';
import { legal, salesReady } from '../../config/legal';
import { guide, formatPrice } from '../../config/offers';
const e = legal.editor;
---

<LegalLayout title="Terms of sale" description="Terms of sale for the Cycle Awakening guide and online offers.">
  {!salesReady && (
    <p class="prelaunch" role="note">
      No sales are open at the moment. The terms below are a working draft; they will be completed and published before
      sales open.
    </p>
  )}
  <h2>1. Purpose and scope</h2>
  <p>
    These terms govern sales made on the Cycle Awakening website between <Val v={e.name} /> (“Cycle Awakening”) and any
    individual acting for non-professional purposes (“the customer”). They are accepted when the order is placed and can be
    downloaded or printed from this page.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Seller</h2>
  <p>
    <Val v={e.name} />, <Val v={e.legalFormEn} />, <Val v={e.addressEn} />, <Val v={e.registrationEn} />, VAT {e.vatNumber}.
    Contact: <a href={`mailto:${e.email}`}>{e.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Products</h2>
  <h3>3.1 The Guide (digital content)</h3>
  <p>
    “{guide.name}” is a digital book{guide.pages ? ` of ${guide.pages} pages` : ''}, with printable tools.
    It is provided without a physical medium, by download. It is educational lifestyle content: it does not replace
    medical advice and guarantees no results. The Guide is currently written in French.
  </p>
  <h3>3.2 Premium subscription</h3>
  <p>
    <Val v="TODO_LEGAL_PREMIUM (section à rédiger à l’ouverture de l’offre : durée, reconduction, essai, prix, résiliation en ligne)" />
  </p>

  <h2>4. Prices</h2>
  <p>
    Prices are shown in euros, including all taxes. The Guide is sold at {formatPrice(guide.priceCents, 'en-GB')}.
    <Val v={e.vatNoteEn} />. The applicable price is the one displayed when the order is placed.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Order and payment</h2>
  <p>
    Orders are placed online via the secure payment page of our provider Stripe. The order is final once payment has been
    validated (order button stating the obligation to pay). A confirmation email summarising the order is sent to the
    address provided. Cycle Awakening does not store any bank details.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Delivery of the Guide</h2>
  <p>
    The Guide is delivered by email, as a personal download link, usually within minutes of payment. This link is valid
    for 7 days and allows 5 downloads. If it does not arrive, the customer can write to
    <a href={`mailto:${e.email}`}>{e.email}</a>: a new link will be sent.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Right of withdrawal</h2>
  <p>The customer in principle has 14 days to withdraw (EU Directive 2011/83/EU; in France, article L221-18 of the Consumer Code).</p>
  <p>
    However, for digital content supplied without a physical medium, this right can no longer be exercised once
    performance has begun with the customer’s <strong>prior express consent</strong> and her <strong>express
    waiver</strong> of her right of withdrawal (Directive 2011/83/EU, article 16; in France, article L221-28, 13° of the Consumer Code). When ordering, the
    customer is asked to tick a box requesting immediate access to the Guide and acknowledging the loss of her right of
    withdrawal. This consent and waiver are confirmed in the order confirmation email.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the customer has not given this consent, she can withdraw within 14 days by writing to
    <a href={`mailto:${e.email}`}>{e.email}</a>; she will then be refunded within 14 days, using the same means of payment.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Legal guarantee of conformity</h2>
  <p>
    The Guide benefits from the legal guarantee of conformity for digital content (EU Directive 2019/770; in France, articles L224-25-1 et seq.
    of the Consumer Code). If the file is defective or unreadable, write to <a href={`mailto:${e.email}`}>{e.email}</a>: a
    compliant version will be provided or, failing that, the customer will be refunded.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    Cycle Awakening’s content consists of general lifestyle markers. It is not a medical act and does not take individual
    medical circumstances into account. It is up to each person to consult a health professional about any symptom,
    treatment or particular situation (pregnancy, illness, ongoing treatment).
  </p>

  <h2>10. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The Guide is reserved for the customer’s personal use. Any reproduction, distribution, resale or sharing, even free of
    charge, is prohibited.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Personal data</h2>
  <p>Data collected when ordering is processed in accordance with the <a href="/en/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>12. Complaints and mediation</h2>
  <p>
    Any complaint can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${e.email}`}>{e.email}</a>. If a disagreement persists, the customer may
    contact the <Val v={legal.mediator.nameEn} /> free of charge, which helps consumers with cross-border disputes within the
    European Union: <a href={legal.mediator.website}>{legal.mediator.website.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of Cyprus. This choice does not deprive the customer of the protection afforded
    by the mandatory provisions of the law of her country of residence (EU “Rome I” Regulation, article 6). Failing an
    amicable solution, the customer may bring proceedings before the courts of her country of residence.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>

<style>
  .prelaunch { font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium); }
</style>
